Title: 0004-savefile-check-fclose
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0003-construct-simsprite.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-16
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic - any platform; upstream candidate

Problem:
  saveFile() ignores the result of fclose(), so a final buffer-flush error (full disk, I/O error) is reported as a successful save; the caller believes the city is safe on disk when it may be truncated or incomplete.
Solution:
  Return false when fclose() fails. Upstream-worthy: the change is data-safety, no behavior change on the success path. Atomicity against the existing save is handled in the frontend via a temp file + rename, so fopen(wb) only ever truncates the temp file.
Validation:
  not-run
Removal:
  Fill in when this is a workaround; permanent fixes say so here.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
index 30e91a0..e2b4c80 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/fileio.cpp
@@ -296,7 +296,11 @@ bool Micropolis::loadFileData(const std::string &filename)
         memset(mopBase, 0, WORLD_W * WORLD_H * sizeof(short));
     }
 
-    fclose(f);
+    /* fclose() flushes the final buffer - an error there (e.g. a full
+     * disk) must not be reported as a successful save. */
+    if (fclose(f) != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
 
     return result;
 }
@@ -458,7 +462,11 @@ bool Micropolis::saveFile(const std::string &filename)
         save_short(((short *)&map[0][0]), WORLD_W * WORLD_H, f) &&
         save_short(((short *)&mop[0][0]), WORLD_W * WORLD_H, f);
 
-    fclose(f);
+    /* fclose() flushes the final buffer - an error there (e.g. a full
+     * disk) must not be reported as a successful save. */
+    if (fclose(f) != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
 
     return result;
 }
